  "body": "# Fix MonarchTokenizer.getLoadStatus infinite loop on circular language embedding\n\nFixes microsoft/monaco-editor#5026\n\n## Problem Summary\nWhen calling `monaco.editor.colorize()`, if `Lang1` embeds `Lang2` and `Lang2` embeds `Lang1`, the resulting call to `MonarchTokenizer.getLoadStatus()` enters an infinite recursive loop. This exceeds the call stack limit and crashes the tokenization process.\n\n## Root Cause\n`MonarchTokenizer.getLoadStatus()` previously resolved its `_embeddedLanguages` by synchronously invoking `getLoadStatus()` on any instantiated nested `MonarchTokenizer`. Because it did not track which languages had already been evaluated during the resolution pass, cyclic dependencies caused it to traverse the graph infinitely.\n\n## Fix Summary\nIntroduced standard DFS cycle-detection via an optional `visited: Set<string>` parameter in `getLoadStatus()`. \n- If the current `_languageId` is already in the `visited` set, the traversal correctly breaks the cycle and returns `{ loaded: true }`.\n- This delegates the resolution of pending promises to the original caller further up the stack, successfully aggregating all transitive nested dependencies without redundant traversal.\n\n## Validation Performed\n- **Regression Test:** Added `test('Ensure MonarchTokenizer.getLoadStatus() does not infinite loop on circular language embedding')` to `monarch.test.ts`. This test specifically wires two tokenizers to `nextEmbedded` into each other and guarantees that `tokenizer1.getLoadStatus()` evaluates successfully to `loaded: true` instead of throwing a `RangeError`.\n- **Backward Compatibility:** Because `visited` is initialized with a default parameter, external callers tracking `instanceof MonarchTokenizer` remain fully compatible.\n- **Diff constraints:** Maintained minimal diff and zero unrelated refactoring.\n",
  "rebaseable": true
 },
